in 2013  a 330 000 hamburger received worldwide  attention  why it was grown in a lab  researchers and entrepreneurs joined  forces to create  cultured meat an innovation that can  satisfy your taste buds  without the environmental or ethical  worries associated with traditional  animal agriculture  cultured meat which goes by many names  is real  meat that is produced by in vitro cell  cultures  first scientists obtain a muscle sample  from a live animal  next cells are extracted from the sample  and bathed in a nutrient-rich growth  medium  that allows them to proliferate  exponentially  given that the industry is relatively  new there are challenges cultured meat  must  tackle to become a staple on our dinner  plates  one obstacle is replicating the textures  and shapes  of animal grown meat to overcome this  scientists are experimenting with  growing meat on scaffolds  which encourage cells to form into  specific structures  another challenge is that growing  cultivated meat is relatively costly  but since the lab-grown burger's first  debut  expenses have fallen dramatically and  continue to do so  thanks to the dedication of researchers  and entrepreneurs  cultured meat would one day help be the  world's growing population  in more ethical and sustainable ways  [Music]  you
 

